/-!
# Stacks 05WY: flatness on the fibre over a field-valued point

Work in Situation 05WX: morphisms `f : X ⟶ Y` and `h : Y ⟶ Z` of algebraic spaces over a scheme
`S`, a quasi-coherent `𝒪_X`-module `F` and a point `x ∈ |X|`.  For a field-valued point
`x : Spec(K) ⟶ X` in the class of `x` put `z = h ∘ f ∘ x`, let `X_z = Spec(K) ×_{z, Z} X` and
`Y_z = Spec(K) ×_{z, Z} Y` be the fibres, `f_z : X_z ⟶ Y_z` the induced morphism and `F_z` the
pullback of `F` to `X_z`.  Condition (2) of Stacks 05WY is that `F_z` is flat over `Y_z` at the
`K`-rational point of `X_z` determined by `x`, in the sense of Stacks 05VV.  This file proves
that it is equivalent to condition (1), the geometric-stalk condition
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsFibreFlatOverAtGeometricPoint`, for every geometric point `x̄` over
`x` and every representative `x`; in particular neither condition depends on these choices.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.fieldPointFibreSource`, `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.fieldPointFibreTarget`
  and `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.fieldPointFibreMap`: the fibres `X_z`, `Y_z` and `f_z`, as fibre
  products of algebraic spaces (Stacks 02X2).
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.fieldPointFibrePoint`: the `K`-rational point of `X_z` determined by
  `x`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsFlatOnFibreAtFieldValuedPoint`: condition (2) of Stacks 05WY.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isFlatOnFibreAtFieldValuedPoint_iff_isFibreFlatOverAtGeometricPoint`:
  **Stacks 05WY, (1) `⟺` (2).**
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isFlatOverAtGeometricPoint_fieldPointFibreMap_iff`: the same at one
  geometric point of `X_z`, which is where the mathematics is.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isFibreFlatOverAtGeometricPoint_iff_of_image_eq`: condition (1) does
  not depend on the geometric point over `x`.
* `Module.flatQuotSMul_iff_flat_of_tensorProduct_flat`: the commutative algebra.

## Implementation notes

Write `B`, `C` for the étale local rings of `Y`, `X` at `ȳ`, `x̄` and `B'`, `C'` for those of
`Y_z`, `X_z` at points above them, and `J` for the ideal of `B` generated by the maximal ideal of
the étale local ring of `Z`.  The three cartesian squares `Y_z = Spec(K) ×_Z Y`,
`X_z = Spec(K) ×_Z X` and `X_z = Y_z ×_Y X` give, through the cartesian input of Stacks 05VW
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.cartesian_etaleStalk_tensor_flat`), flatness of `B/J → B'` and of
`C/JC → C'` and flatness of `C'` over `C ⊗_B B'`.  The étale local ring of `Spec(K)` is a field
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isField_etaleLocalRing_yoneda`), which is what makes `J` die in `B'`
and `C'`: no flatness of `Spec(K) ⟶ Z` is used.  The geometric stalk of `F_z` is `C' ⊗_C F_{x̄}`
by Stacks 05VQ.  Then `F_{x̄}/J F_{x̄}` flat over `B/J` gives `C' ⊗_C F_{x̄}` flat over `B'` by
base change, and conversely Stacks 0584 (2) over the faithfully flat local map `C/JC → C'` gives
the descent.  Condition (2) is read through Stacks 05VU at a geometric point of `X_z`, the
pullback being quasi-coherent by Stacks 03GA.

That condition (1) does not depend on the geometric point is proved with the equivalence itself:
two geometric points over `x` are dominated by a third, and a geometric point dominating `x̄`
lifts to the fibre over the field-valued point `x̄` itself, at the same `K`-rational point as the
tautological lift of `x̄`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 05WY](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05WY)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 05WX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05WX)
